==Faroese==

===Etymology===
From {{der|fo|non|góðr}}, from {{der|fo|gem-pro|*gōdaz}}, from {{der|fo|ine-pro|*gʰedʰ-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|fo|/ˈkɔuːwʊɹ/}}
*: {{rhymes|fo|ɔuːwʊɹ}}

===Adjective===
{{fo-adj|betri|bestur}}

# [[good]]
#* Genesis 1:31 ([http://www.biblian.fo/default.asp?gerd=visbok&bokid=1&kapitulid=1 Faroese Bible])
#*: {{quote|fo|Og Gud sá alt tað, ið Hann hevði gjørt - og tað var sera gott. Og kvøld varð, og morgun varð, sætta dag.|God saw all that he had made, and it was very '''good'''. And there was evening, and there was morning—the sixth day.}}

====Declension====
{{fo-decl-adj-16|g|ó|o}}

====Antonyms====
* {{l|fo|ringur}}, {{l|fo|illur}} (bad)

====Derived terms====
{{der3|fo
|góðan morgun<t:good morning>
|góðan dag<t:good day>
|gott kvøld<t:good evening>
|góða nátt<t:good night>
|góða ólavsøku<t:good St. Olav's Day>
}}

==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|góðr}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*gōdaz}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*gʰedʰ-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈkouːðʏr/}}
* {{audio|is|Is-góður.oga}}
*: {{rhymes|is|ouːðʏr|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{is-adj|@@}}

# [[good]]
#* Genesis 1:31 ([http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Fyrsta%20b%C3%B3k%20M%C3%B3se+1:31&version=ICELAND Icelandic Bible], [http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Fyrsta%20b%C3%B3k%20M%C3%B3se%201:31&version=NIV New International Version])
#*: {{quote|is|Og Guð leit allt, sem hann hafði gjört, og sjá, það var harla '''gott'''. Það varð kveld og það varð morgunn, hinn sjötti dagur.|God saw all that he had made, and it was very '''good'''. And there was evening, and there was morning—the sixth day.}}
# to taste good
#: {{uxi|is|[[takk fyrir matinn|Takk fyrir matinn]], hann var '''góður'''.|Thank you for the meal, it was very tasty.}}
# [[proficient]], good at something
#: {{uxi|is|Hann er '''góður''' á gítar.|He is a proficient guitar player.}}
#: {{syn|is|fær}}
# [[kind]] to, [[kindhearted]]
#: {{uxi|is|Hann er '''góður''' við börn.|He is kind to children.}}
# [[well-behaved]]; able to keep [[calm]]
#: {{uxi|is|Hundurinn minn er mjög '''góður'''.|My dog is very well-behaved.}}
#: {{uxi|is|Krakkar, nú verðið þið að vera [[þægur|þæg]] og góð.|Kids, now you must behave well and stay calm.}}
#: {{syn|is|þægur}}
# a [[considerable]] amount; a [[significant]] amount
#: {{uxi|is|Maður verður að gefa sér '''góðan''' tíma til þess.|One has to set aside a considerable amount of time for that.}}
# {{lb|is|colloquial}} [[satisfied]] or [[at ease]]
#: {{uxi|is|Má bjóða þér kaffi? – Nei takk, ég er '''góður'''.|Can I offer you some coffee? – No thanks, I'm good.}}

